/// known-gap: interp cell references have no fields (the interpreter is being retired)
/// A cell reference, as `:grid_neighbors` gives them, has its place: `>> x`,
/// `>> y`, and the grid's name `>> grid`.
:grid("map", 3, 3)
:grid_void("map", 1, 0)
repeat :grid_neighbors("map", 1, 1) as n
    :say("{n >> grid} {n >> x},{n >> y}")
xx
